// TEST: Juxtaposed Statement (rejects)
// ERROR: BL1001 @ 10:11
// ERROR-CONTAINS: Expected the end of the statement
// Two expressions side by side on one line have no meaning in Blade (no
// implicit multiplication, and application needs parentheses). The parser
// used to end the `let` at `1` and read `b` as a SECOND top-level statement:
// a = 1, plus a printed bare `b` -- silently. The terminator rule (formalism
// §15.1) requires a newline, `;` or a closer after every statement and
// refuses anything else, at the offending token.
let b = 3
let a = 1 b
